{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-e517725503967e2d30a6","statement":"Note that Theorem <<ref:singularity>> implies\nnilpotent orbits of $\\GL_n$ and the minimal nilpotent orbit of a general semisimple Lie algebra $\\frakg$ are normal, Cohen-Macaulay, Gorenstein, and have rational singularities.\nThis is not true for the general nilpotent orbits in semisimple Lie algebras, which implies that the above relation between transversal slices an nilpotent orbits does not extend to the general case.","source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","statement_sha256":"1f558defb77b911d6480c11289fd7f7fefaa0357f295f0290eccf8410bfb1449","kind":"remark","label":"Remark 77","ref_key":"","name":"","order":99,"deps":[{"ref":"singularity","card_id":"ma-c-83360aeb082e28f99e8a","label":"Theorem 63","resolved":true,"target":"card"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"9aa0de800bec9f56ae36a0522194f91bc11ab1fe49bff0d4068568a9eb549a68","line":1646,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-27T16:49:20+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":423,"math_hints":6}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","title":"Guide for Lecturers in the Park City Mathematics Institute","abstract":"We introduce various affine Grassmannians, study their geometric properties, and give some applications. We also discuss the geometric Satake equivalence. These are the expanded lecture notes for a mini-course in 2015 PCMI summer school. References updated and more details added.","authors":["Xinwen Zhu"],"year":"2016","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","macros":{"on":"\\operatorname","fraka":"{\\mathfrak a}","frakg":"{\\mathfrak g}","frakl":"{\\mathfrak l}","frakp":"{\\mathfrak p}","frakq":"{\\mathfrak q}","fraks":"{\\mathfrak s}","frak